# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. cargo-fuzz's template ignores it,
# which is the right default for a library but wrong here: this package is a
# detached workspace whose transitive kin-* dependencies resolve from the Kin
# registry, so an ignored lock left every run to re-resolve against whatever
# was newest and let a fuzz build turn red with no change to this repository.
# The lock is tracked, and the workflow proves the build resolved through it.
